{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508790-any-ideas-for-an-alternate-toreador-bane","id":1508790,"title":"Any ideas for an alternate Toreador bane?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-18T16:13:51-07:00","id":1508790,"title":"Any ideas for an alternate Toreador bane?","content":"I find the standard bane kind of a pain to enforce, and not very engaging or fun to roleplay. And the official alternate is wretched.<br /> <br /> I don't know. Maybe a bane that makes them look more like a statue than a person? Anyone have any other ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T16:43:23-07:00","id":1508792,"title":"","content":"How about if they are more addicted to blood due to their hunger for life so they need to suck more often, like every time the toreador uses the vitae for something he must make a difficulty 6 willpower roll to see if he doesn't have abstinence, failing the roll causes him to lose one die on every roll that requires concentration.<br /> <br /> Another option is something like the Changeling Sidhe, every time they meet a new mortal who has a preference for the Toreador's gender he makes a Fainity roll difficulty 8, if he doesn't get any success, he becomes obsessed with the Toreador and may even turn a stalker or something.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T23:41:49-07:00","id":1508849,"title":"","content":"I do not like the standard Toreador bane either. <br /> Fortunately, banes are easy to design as they should just always scale with bane severity. <br /> <br /> Object of desire; anyone trying to recognize, remember or describe the Toreador adds their Bane Severity dice to a roll. Likewise they add that amount of dice to resist any power to erase their presence, be it by Obfuscate, or memory changes.<br /> <br /> Statuesque; the Toreador looks slightly to perfect and when remaining still has some semblance to a statue, or perhaps wax-doll by the way humans see it. This subconsciously attracts most Kine, and the Toreador faces their bane severity to all rolls to remain hidden, veil themselves with obfuscate, disguise themselves or have memory of them erased.<br /> <br /> Close to the Kine; whenever the Toreador tastes a fleeting, intense or acute temperament when they hunt, they suffer their Bane Severity to any actions not in line with the temperament they just tasted. This lasts until either daybreak or the Toreador has lost a hunger to rousing the blood in an action in line with the temperament.<br /> An alternative could be that the Toreador has one favored temperament, and takes their Bane in penalties to all rolls for the reminder of the night for drinking from another temperament, but that might overlap a bit much with the Ventrue (another bane I dislike, but that is another question!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel","name":"Trassel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T08:28:20-07:00","id":1508892,"title":"","content":"Maybe a Weakness or Bane along these lines :<br /> <br /> If a Toreador Vampiress or Toreador Vampire fails a Social Attributes roll ( or for instance a SAs extended action ) then they lose a point o Temporary Willpower. Maybe the penalty could be a different resources or quality. This Weakness or Bane could also be used for Toreador Ghouls and Revenants related to Toreador Vampires.<br /> <br /> Also there is the option of using the banes or limitations listed as possible about any Vampiress or Vampire. There are many of them listed in VtM supplements and books, and they are definitely varied.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T12:40:56-07:00","id":1508919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trassel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508790-any-ideas-for-an-alternate-toreador-bane?p=1508849#post1508849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Object of desire; anyone trying to recognize, remember or describe the Toreador adds their Bane Severity dice to a roll. Likewise they add that amount of dice to resist any power to erase their presence, be it by Obfuscate, or memory changes.<br /> <br /> Statuesque; the Toreador looks slightly to perfect and when remaining still has some semblance to a statue, or perhaps wax-doll by the way humans see it. This subconsciously attracts most Kine, and the Toreador faces their bane severity to all rolls to remain hidden, veil themselves with obfuscate, disguise themselves or have memory of them erased.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like these. I think I may use Statuesque in my next game.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T18:11:49-07:00","id":1508958,"title":"","content":"I thought of doubling down on the Anne Rice aspect of Toreador design with the &quot;can't drink dead blood.&quot;<br /> <br /> From the VC wiki:<br /> <b>Dead Blood:</b> Vampires are vulnerable to the consumption of dead blood. It can weaken them severely for several weeks if consumed in a small amount or if a decent amount is consumed, it can outright kill them, especially if it was consumed right when a vampire was feeding on their prey and didn\u2019t stop before their heart gave out, their prey\u2019s death flowing into them as well\u200b.<br /> <br /> Ventrue and Giovanni also have feeding issues, so it might feel redundant or it might reflect the Toreador's &quot;love of life&quot; facet. In the V5 world, it would also exclude them from Bagger and Farmer PTs, and might possibly make dropping Hunger to 0 with a kill a very delicate endeavor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T05:46:32-07:00","id":1509170,"title":"","content":"You seem happy with Trassel's suggestions and I agree that they're pretty on point for the Clan. For my part, I'd probably use Object of Desire or some variation of it rather than Statuesque since the latter's a little too specific about Toreador appearances for my tastes, but either way, attracting too much attention is both very appropriate for them and something that's hard to completely shrug off. Even setting aside stuff like frenzies, messy criticals, and bestial failures that you really won't want to be remembered in any kind of detail for, canny enemies/rivals can find all sorts of ways to turn this sort of Bane to their advantage.<br /> <br /> A fairly simple Bane occurs to me for Toreador Antitribu-types.<br /> <br /> <b>Cruel Catharsis:</b> The passions of some Degenerates become so inextricably bound up with their own predatory urges that they find it difficult to rouse their spirits without abusing and humiliating others. Toreadors of this stripe must have inflicted an amount of Health and/or Willpower Damage to one or more other individuals that is greater than or equal to their Bane Severity during the same scene; any distribution between Health and Willpower Damage will suffice. This can be Superficial or Aggravated Damage if the Toreador is recovering from Superficial Willpower Damage, but if they are recovering from Aggravated Willpower Damage, at least half of this minimum amount must consist of Aggravated Damage (round up). Willpower regained through the indulgence of Compulsions is not subject to this restriction*.<br /> <br /> *I just threw this in there to encourage them to be more friendly with their Beasts in general and provide at least a little bit of extra room for varied playstyles, but it could easily be cut out.<br /> <br /> Here's another one, more in the vein of love potions and other supernatural charms working a bit too well. I have some doubts about penalizing something so fundamental to Toreador themes, but it did seem somewhat appropriate and I wanted to try writing it out anyway.<br /> <br /> <b>Fatal Attraction:</b> Certain Divas find themselves becoming the victims of their own charms, inflaming others' passions to the extent that they become uncontrollable. When such Toreadors succeed in using supernatural abilities to directly manipulate the emotions of others, a number of dice from the target's dice pool equal to the Toreador's margin of win or Bane Severity (whichever is lower) are converted into Hunger dice for the remainder of the scene or until the supernatural effect ends (whichever comes first); even mortals are subject to this effect, and it stacks with Hunger dice rolled from actual Hunger levels. Toreador blood bonds are similarly volatile, though in this case the associated number of Hunger dice is based on the thrall's Bond Strength or the Diva's Bane Severity (whichever is lower).<br /> Presence powers are subject to this Bane without exception, as are Social rolls that are augmented with Blood Surges. However, insights from Auspex can be leveraged without running afoul of this Bane, and the Bane does not apply to outright mind control, such as via Dominate.<br /> <br /> I mentioned the possibility of a Resonance-based spin on the VTR Daeva Bane in the V5 Player's Guide thread, though I do wonder whether it might be a hassle to keep track of all the mortal infatuations that pop up.<br /> <br /> <b>Ensnaring Passions:</b> Some Toreadors require not only blood but intense emotions to sustain them. Such Toreadors gain the Addiction Flaw, but in this case, the addiction is to blood with an Intense or Acute temperament (the specific Resonance doesn't matter) and the penalties can stack over multiple feedings that don't satisfy the addiction, up to a maximum equal to their Bane Severity. To make matters worse, when these Toreadors feed on blood that satisfies their addiction, they risk becoming obsessed with their prey. Treat blood of the appropriate types as vitae for the purpose of establishing or intensifying blood bonds, and neither the Unbondable Merit nor blood bonds to Kindred protect against this effect; bonus dice from Bond Resistance can apply to rolls to resist the influence of blood bonds as usual, but they are rolled as Hunger dice in this case, with even successful resistance potentially resulting in horrific crimes of passion. The maximum Bond Strength possible through this Bane is equal to the Toreador's Bane Severity, and they can spend a point of Willpower while feeding to prevent mortal blood from contributing to a blood bond. Increase this Willpower cost by one point when the Toreador feeds on blood with an Acute temperament or if they slake at least three Hunger levels while feeding, or by two points if both conditions apply. Willpower cannot be spent to avert this effect at all while subject to a Hunger Compulsion or in the midst of a hunger frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27894,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27894-paramecius","user":"Paramecius","date":". 04-21-2023, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27894-paramecius","name":"Paramecius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27894_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}